2) PW crack 4
- the challange was identical to PW crack 3 with the exception of being 100 possible solutions
- it was a great opportunity to solidify my pipe and redirection skills in linux
- with the tr command i replaced spaces with new lines and removed " and ,
- command:  tr ' ' '\n' < raw_passwords.txt  | tr -d '" ,' > clean_passwords.txt 
- after that i wanted to automate the process of running the script and insering the passwords after the command ran
- i asked gemini to teach me shell scripting and i also wrote my 1st script myself
- this is the following script:
while read -r password; do
  python3 level4.py >>results.txt <<<"$password"
done <clean_passwords.txt
- after i gave it rights and ran it i used cat results.txt | grep pico to find the flag
//
-flag: picoCTF{fl45h_5pr1ng1ng_d770d48c}
//
- i learned about the shell scripting
- python3 level4.py >>results.txt <<<"$password" the 1st argument is a command i executed, on the middle is the file i am outputing the result from a command to with >> and 
and <<< "$password" is a variable from the while loop i am passing into the script after it executes in this case.
//
